{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the synthesis and characterization of a nonoxidovanadium(IV) complex [VIVL] (1) using a sterically hindered Mannich base ligand. This complex acts as a highly efficient, reusable, and green catalyst for the one-pot multicomponent synthesis of 2-amino-3-cyano-4H-pyrans, 4H-chromenes, biscoumarins, and xanthenes in ethanol. Mechanistic studies revealed that the reaction pathway (Type-I vs. Type-II) is dictated by the specific 1,3-dicarbonyl compound and the electronic nature of the aldehyde substituents.",
